= History
// Just the biggest events that most people in the modern day would know about

== The Golden Age
What records remain suggest that the old world of #term[Makkeo] was similar to ours, but had made great leaps in technology.
Research into #term[Mana Gates] led the Old World to discover a seemingly infinite energy source, which propelled the world into a golden age.

However, cracks began to form near the end of this time period.
Protests broke out about the etchical problems with the technology behind #term[Mana Gates], with "Quietus Cells" being mentioned in multiple records.
// Quietus Cells being the capsules used to trap escaping souls

The real tipping point came some decades later it seems, when spontaneous #term[Mutations] became known to the world at large.
The brakes on development were pushed due to public outcry, but the damage was already done, and there was no way back.

== The Collapse
Mana saturation in the atmoshphere was at this point so high that #term[Mana Gates] started manifesting at random. 
Additionally, creatures started emerging from them; most dangerously, the first #term[Titans]. Cities started falling to their rampages, the water started drying up (except in Mana Zones, they remained strangely unaffected), and mutation accelerated worldwide. Many retreated to the growing arid regions to avoid mutation, but that's a hard lifestyle that killed as many as monsters in Mana Zones.

== Sanctuary's Founding
After many hard years, a source of potable water outside Mana Zones was found, and hte scattered survivors gradually congealed to form the first major post-Collapse settlement of Sanctuary. Over time, Mana came to be a well-understood phenomenon, and Mana-Tech saw widespread adoption in Sanctuary.

== [Second Moon] Darkens
After an eclipse, [Second Moon], Makkeo's Second Moon remained darkened, growing spiky and ominous, revealing the truly Cosmic ramifications of the Collapse and shattering religions.

== Destruction of Sanctuary
Though it was believed that Sanctuary had found a way to safely harness Mana for their technology, their confidence turned out to have been misplaced. Aberrants and Titanspawn converged on the great city and it fell to ruin, a crushing defeat to the symbol of human perseverance to most.

== First Titan Falls
To the Ahadi, the Destruction of Sanctuary marked an important turning point. More and more people flocked to their ranks in the hopes of finally fighting back against the Titans. Using all means available to them, the group fought to bring about the Titanslayer thier founder spoke of long ago, and were finally successful. Sorin Fajiri, a young warrior with tremendous command of Mana, aided by the sacrifice of many Ahadi, was able to kill the Titan Aspirena, a desert-dwelling, Anomalocaris-shaped colossus capable of flight.

== Exploration of Sanctuary
Invigorated by the fall of the first Titan, adventuring groups gradually began successfully delving the monster-infested ruins of Sanctuary, recovering the lost Mana-Tech, and proving that there was a lot to be gained from such expeditions.

== The Crowning
// I'd fully forgot that a Titan died here. Will probably have to reconcile a bit with the Ahadi and The Titanslayer stuff.
A turf war between Hunter guilds at Prey's End spiraled out into a grand bet. The greatest Hunting Parties of each Guild attended, and on the anniversary of the death of the First Titan they set out ot prove their guild the best and most profitable. This started a yearly tradition called the Crowning, where adventurers prove their mettle, with the greatest rewards promised to those who can finally slay the Second Titan.

