= Creatures
== Titans
#term("Titans", is_definition: true) are the apex creatures of the world.
Closely tied to the #term("Mana Gates") they came through, they distort the space around them and force the environment to suit their traits, creating #term[Mana Zones].

#term[Titans] rarely wander far from areas of dense #term[Mana], and two live #term[Titans] haven't been observed in the same #term("Mana Zone", key: "Mana Zones").
The [TODO area where two titans fought and shit] suggests it might still be possible for two to occupy the same area at the same time, though this remains contested.

== Titanspawn
#term("Titanspawn", is_definition: true) are creatures either stemming from a #term("Titan", key: "Titans"), or from a #term("Mana Gate", key: "Mana Gates") directly.
They seem resistant to #term[Mutations], and like #term[Titans] don't seem to wander far from #term[Mana Zones], but their otherworldy nature makes them no less of a threat to #term[Hunters] in the wild.

== Aberrants
#term("Aberrants", is_definition: true) are creatures of the world mutated until they've lost their sense of self.
Some maintain a semblance of their former selves, in either personality or visage, though many are so mutated that it's even difficult to tell what sort of creature they were to begin with.


